:"205","job_location":"73","job_city":"74","job_state":"75","job_country":"76","job_latitude":41.88325,"job_longitude":-87.6323879,"job_benefits":"206","job_benefits_strings":"207","job_google_link":"208","job_salary":null,"job_salary_string":"209","job_min_salary":114000,"job_max_salary":164000,"job_salary_period":"210","job_highlights":"211","job_onet_soc":null,"job_onet_job_zone":null,"employer_reviews":null,"job_uid":"212"},{},{"item":0},{"item":0},"","Senior Full Stack Java Developer","Eliassen Group","https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQbGF7xRIpaJPvSVecTvI-W8LTW7pkYyMmrn0kV&s=0","https://www.eliassen.com","LinkedIn","Contractor",["213"],"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/senior-full-stack-java-developer-at-eliassen-group-4445538857",["214"],"Description\\n\\nRemote\\n\\nOur client is seeking a Senior Full Stack Java Developer to build and support healthcare applications. The role requires hands-on development across backend and frontend with emphasis on healthcare integrations. The developer will deliver end-to-end features, collaborate with clinical and business stakeholders, and operate effectively in a remote environment.\\n\\nDue to client requirements, applicants must be willing and able to work on a w2 basis. For our w2 consultants, we offer a great benefits package that includes Medical, Dental, and Vision benefits, 401k with company matching, and life insurance.\\n\\nRate: $70.00 to $80.00/hr. w2\\n\\nResponsibilities\\n\\n• Design, develop, test, and deploy Java and Spring Boot services, REST APIs, and microservices.\\n• Build and enhance web and mobile user interfaces using Angular and/or React, with React Native preferred.\\n• Implement integration workflows for healthcare data exchange including HL7 and FHIR.\\n• Develop and maintain interfaces using tools such as Mirth Connect.\\n• Create and optimize SQL queries and schemas for relational databases.\\n• Containerize and run applications using Docker and Tomcat where appropriate.\\n• Own features from requirements through production support and troubleshooting.\\n• Collaborate with clinical teams, QA, and cross-functional stakeholders to clarify needs and validate solutions.\\n• Document designs, APIs, and operational procedures following best practices.\\n• Participate in issue tracking and sprint activities using Jira or similar tools.\\n\\nExperience Requirements\\n\\n• 7-10+ years of professional software development experience with a hands-on focus.\\n• Expertise in Java, Spring/Spring Boot, REST APIs, microservices, and web application development.\\n• Front-end experience with Angular and/or React; React Native preferred.\\n• Strong SQL skills and relational database experience.\\n• Experience with Tomcat and Docker.\\n• Healthcare interoperability experience with HL7 and FHIR, including data exchange.\\n• Integration experience with Mirth Connect and healthcare data transformation.\\n• Background integrating with insurance, financial, laboratory, and clinical systems; familiarity with Quest and Labcorp interfaces preferred.\\n• Nice to have: medical device integrations and knowledge of ASTM protocols and device communication standards.\\n• Proven troubleshooting ability and independent problem-solving in production environments.\\n• Effective communication with technical and non-technical stakeholders in a remote setting.\\n• Understanding of SDLC, unit testing, documentation, and collaboration with QA.\\n• Cloud exposure is a plus; DevOps/cloud handled by dedicated teams.\\n\\nEducation Requirements","12 hours ago","2026-07-31T20:00:00.000Z","Chicago, IL","Chicago","Illinois","US",["215","216"],["217","218"],"https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3D3oMMzpGnQmVjhOFyAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"3oMMzpGnQmVjhOFyAAAAAA==","","Developer - Information Technology","United Airlines","https://t0.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&url=https://united.com&size=128","https://www.united.com","United Airlines Jobs","Full-time",["219"],"https://careers.united.com/us/en/job/WHQ00026621/Developer-Information-Technology",["220"],"Achieving our goals starts with supporting yours. Grow your career, access top-tier health and wellness benefits, build lasting connections with your team and our customers, and travel the world using our extensive route network.\\n\\nCome join us to create what’s next. Let’s define tomorrow, together.\\n\\nDescription\\nDescription - External\\nUnited's Digital Technology team is comprised of many talented individuals all working together with cutting-edge technology to build the best airline in the history of aviation. Our team designs, develops and maintains massively scaling technology solutions brought to life with innovative architectures, data analytics, and digital solutions.\\n\\nJob overview and responsibilities\\nWe are seeking a Developer to build and enhance features within our Internal Developer Portal while supporting the evolution of United’s API ecosystem. This role will focus on developing developer-facing capabilities, owning and improving the Kong API platform, and applying site reliability engineering practices to increase platform stability, observability, and operational excellence. The ideal candidate brings strong software engineering experience, API platform expertise, and a reliability-focused mindset to help application teams deliver secure, scalable, and resilient services.\\n• Develop and enhance features within the Internal Developer Portal to improve developer self-service, API discoverability, onboarding, and platform adoption.\\n\\n• Own, support, and continuously improve the Kong API platform, including gateway configuration, API routing, policies, plugins, security controls, and operational standards.\\n\\n• Partner with application teams to design, publish, secure, and manage APIs using scalable patterns that support consistency, governance, and reliability across the API ecosystem.\\n\\n• Build reusable developer experiences, templates, documentation, and automation that make it easier for teams to provision, deploy, monitor, and operate API services.\\n\\n• Apply site reliability engineering practices to improve availability, observability, incident response, performance, and operational readiness for platform and API services.\\n\\n• Define and maintain standards for API development, platform components, deployment practices, security, and maintainability across developer-facing capabilities.\\n\\n• Monitor platform health, identify reliability risks, troubleshoot production issues, and drive continuous improvement through automation, logging, metrics, and alerting.\\n\\n• Collaborate with product, architecture, security, and operations stakeholders to align the API platform and developer portal roadmap with organizational priorities.\\n\\n• Lead technical discussions, demos, Lunch and Learn sessions, and workshops to help internal application teams adopt API platform capabilities, developer portal features, and SRE best practices.\\n\\nQualifications\\nWhat’s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\\n• Bachelor’s degree\\n\\n• Computer science, systems analysis or a related field preferred\\n\\n• 2 + years of experience in software engineering with strong focus on cloud-native development and infrastructure automation.\\n\\n• Hands-on expertise in AWS services and architecture, with deep knowledge of Infrastructure as a Code using AWS CDK\\n\\n• Proficient in at least one application development languages (.NET, Java, python, JavaScript, or Go), with ability to support cross-functional teams consuming platform tools and libraries.\\n\\n• Experience building or contributing to internal platform or developer portals using React and TypeScript\\n\\n• Proven ability to collaborate with software teams and guide them in adopting platform tools and best practices\\n\\n• Strong understanding of cloud security, IAM, cost optimization and operational excellence in an AWS environment\\n\\n• Experience optimizing applications, both stand-alone and in distributed systems to maximize performance\\n\\n• Excellent communication skills with experience in leading technical discussion, documentations, and knowledge sharing sessions\\n\\n• Ability to balance hands-on development with strategic planning and technical leadership\\n\\n• Must be legally authorized to work in the United States for any employer without sponsorship\\n\\nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\\n• Cloud technologies (i.e., Azure, AWS)\\n• Dev Ops Experience\\n• Infrastructure knowledge\\n\\nThe base pay range for this role is $89,965.00 to $117,212.00.\\nThe base salary range/hourly rate listed is dependent on job-related, factors such as experience, education, and skills. This position is also eligible for bonus and/or long-term incentive compensation awards.\\n\\nYou may be eligible for the following competitive benefits: medical, dental, vision, life, accident & disability, parental leave, employee assistance program, commuter, paid holidays, paid time off, 401(k) and flight privileges.\\n\\nUnited Airlines is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We recruit, employ, train, compensate, and promote without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. We provide reasonable accommodations for applicants and employees with disabilities. To request an accommodation, contact JobAccommodations@united.com","5 days ago","2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z",["221","216","215"],["222","218","217"],"https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DlqO1pHO2G2bpk3QpAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"lqO1pHO2G2bpk3QpAAAAAA==","","Remote Software Engineer","Turing","https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSB8MIRTbURw2wdAT5uRdblABEzJYT-SeENfUo8&s=0","https://www.turing.com",["213"],"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/remote-software-engineer-at-turing-4446996754",["223"],"About Us\\n\\nBased in San Francisco, California, Turing is the world’s leading research accelerator for frontier AI labs and a trusted partner for global enterprises deploying advanced AI systems. Turing supports customers in two ways: first, by accelerating frontier research with high-quality data, advanced training pipelines, plus top AI researchers who specialize in software engineering, logical reasoning, STEM, multilinguality, multimodality, and agents; and second, by applying that expertise to help enterprises transform AI from proof of concept into proprietary intelligence with systems that perform reliably, deliver measurable impact, and drive lasting results on the P&L.\\n\\nProject Overview\\n\\nAs a Software Engineering evaluator, you will create cutting-edge datasets for training, benchmarking, and advancing large language models, collaborating closely with researchers. This includes curating code examples, providing precise solutions, and making corrections in Python, JavaScript (including ReactJS), C/C++, Java, Rust, and Go; evaluating and refining AI-generated code for efficiency, scalability, and reliability; and working with cross-functional teams to enhance enterprise-level AI-driven coding solutions.\\n\\nWhat Does a Typical Day Look Like?\\n• Working on AI model training initiatives by curating code examples, building solutions, and correcting code in Python, JavaScript (including ReactJS), C/C++, Java, Rust, and Go.\\n• Evaluate and refine AI-generated code to ensure that it is efficient, scalable, and reliable.\\n• Collaborate withcross-functionalteamsto enhance AI-driven coding solutions against industry performance benchmarks.\\n• Build agents that can verify the quality of the code and identify error patterns.\\n• Hypothesize on steps in the software engineering cycle (prototyping, architecture design, API design, production implementation, launch, experiments, monitoring, operational maintenance) and evaluate model capabilities on them\\n• Design verification mechanisms that can automatically verify a solution to a software engineering task.\\n\\nRequired Skills\\n• Several years of software engineering experience (3 years or more)\\n• Strong expertise in building full-stack applications and deploying scalable, production-grade software using modern languages and tools.\\n• Deep understanding of software architecture, design, development, debugging, and code quality/review assessment.\\n• Excellent oral and written communication skills for clear, structured evaluation rationales.\\n\\nEngagement Details\\n• Commitment: flexible engagement, minimum 10 hrs/week, up to 40 hrs/week\\n• Type: Contractor (no medical/paid leave)\\n• Duration: 1 month (potential extensions based on performance and fit)\\n• Location: candidates must be based out of US, Canada or WEU countries (Austria, Belgium, France, Germany, ...)\\n\\nEvaluation Process\\n• The application process takes 15-30 minutes.\\n• Completion of an AI video interview is required.","21 hours ago","2026-07-31T11:00:00.000Z","Anywhere","https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DaRUONLxwqil-Fy4MAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"aRUONLxwqil-Fy4MAAAAAA==","","Remote Senior Software Engineer",["213"],"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/remote-senior-software-engineer-at-turing-4447132334",["224"],"About Us:\\n\\nBased in San Francisco, California, Turing is the world’s leading research accelerator for frontier AI labs and a trusted partner for global enterprises deploying advanced AI systems. Turing supports customers in two ways: first, by accelerating frontier research with high-quality data, advanced training pipelines, plus top AI researchers who specialize in software engineering, logical reasoning, STEM, multilinguality, multimodality, and agents; and second, by applying that expertise to help enterprises transform AI from proof of concept into proprietary intelligence with systems that perform reliably, deliver measurable impact, and drive lasting results on the P&L.\\n\\nIdeal Background:\\n\\nThis role is ideal for engineers who have worked at the frontier of AI — at companies like OpenAI, NVIDIA, Databricks, Palantir, Snowflake, or similar organizations pushing the boundaries of intelligent systems. We especially welcome graduates from top computer science programs such as Stanford, MIT, Carnegie Mellon, UC Berkeley, Georgia Tech, and comparable institutions — though exceptional experience and skill always take precedence over pedigree.\\n\\nProject Overview:\\n\\nAs a Software Engineering evaluator, you will create cutting-edge datasets for training, benchmarking, and advancing large language models, collaborating closely with researchers. This includes curating code examples, providing precise solutions, and making corrections across the full stack — in Python for backend and ML workflows, and JavaScript (React, Node.js) for frontend and API layers, alongside C/C++, Java, Rust, and Go. You will evaluate and refine AI-generated code for efficiency, scalability, and reliability, and work with cross-functional teams to enhance enterprise-level AI-driven coding solutions.\\n\\nWhat Does a Typical Day Look Like?\\n• Work on AI model training initiatives by curating code examples, building solutions, and correcting code across both Python and JavaScript (React, Node.js), with additional work in C/C++, Java, Rust, and Go.\\n• Evaluate and refine AI-generated code across backend and frontend contexts to ensure that it is efficient, scalable, and reliable.\\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to enhance AI-driven coding solutions against industry performance benchmarks.\\n• Build agents that can verify the quality of the code and identify error patterns across full-stack applications.\\n• Hypothesize on steps in the software engineering cycle (prototyping, architecture design, API design, production implementation, launch, experiments, monitoring, operational maintenance) and evaluate model capabilities on them.\\n• Design verification mechanisms that can automatically verify a solution to a software engineering task.\\n\\nRequired Skills:\\n• Several years of software engineering experience (3 years or more)\\n• Strong expertise in building full-stack applications using Python and JavaScript (React, Node.js), with the ability to work across backend and frontend codebases.\\n• Experience deploying scalable, production-grade software using modern languages and tools.\\n• Deep understanding of software architecture, design, development, debugging, and code quality/review assessment.\\n• Excellent oral and written communication skills for clear, structured evaluation rationales.\\n\\nEngagement Details:\\n• Commitment: flexible engagement, minimum 10 hrs/week, up to 40 hrs/week\\n• Type: Contractor (no medical/paid leave)\\n• Duration: 1 month (potential extensions based on performance and fit)\\n• Location: Candidates must be based in the United States\\n\\nEvaluation Process:\\n• The application process takes 15–30 minutes.\\n• Completion of an AI video interview is required.\\n\\nNote: As part of assessments you will go through an AI video interview.\\n\\nAfter applying, you will receive an email with a login link. Please use that link to access the portal and complete your profile.\\n\\nKnow amazing talent? Refer them at turing.com/referrals, and earn money from your network.","20 hours ago","2026-07-31T12:00:00.000Z","https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DHs4jD_5OnaxBp89CAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"Hs4jD_5OnaxBp89CAAAAAA==","","Java Developer","modis","https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSLClhsSk8mvihlkOpII8kDzDT10gLMNbOydTpK&s=0","Akkodis",["213"],"https://www.akkodis.com/en-us/careers/jobs/java-developer-chicago/us_en_6_971574_1640701",["225"],"Akkodis is seeking a Java Developer for a Contract with a client in Chicago, IL (Remote). The ideal candidate will design, develop, and maintain scalable backend applications and microservices while ensuring high performance, reliability, and cloud-native deployment on Azure.\\nRate Range: $41/hour to $42/hour; The rate may be negotiable based on experience, education, geographic location, and other factors.\\nJava Developer Job Responsibilities include:\\n• Design, develop, and maintain scalable backend services and enterprise applications using Java 21+ and Spring Boot.\\n\\n• Build, enhance, and support RESTful APIs and microservices architectures to meet business and customer requirements.\\n\\n• Develop and optimize SQL queries, database structures, and data models to ensure application performance and reliability.\\n\\n• Deploy, monitor, and manage cloud-native applications on Microsoft Azure, including Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS).\\n\\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams in an Agile environment to deliver high-quality software solutions and meet project timelines.\\n\\n• Perform code reviews, implement automated testing, troubleshoot production issues, and contribute to CI/CD and DevOps best practices.\\n\\nRequired Qualifications:\\n• Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related technical field.\\n\\n• 5+ years of experience in Java backend development with a strong focus on enterprise application development.\\n\\n• Hands-on expertise in Java (21+), Spring Boot, REST API development, microservices architecture, and SQL database design and optimization.\\n\\n• Proven experience deploying and managing cloud-native applications on Microsoft Azure, including Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS), with exposure to CI/CD and DevOps practices.\\n\\nIf you are interested in this role, then please click APPLY NOW. For other opportunities available at Akkodis, or any questions, feel free to contact me at Deep.Kumar@akkodisgroup.com.\\n\\nPay Details: $41.00 to $42.00 per hour\\n\\nBenefit offerings available for our associates include medical, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, additional voluntary benefits, EAP program, commuter benefits and a 401K plan. Our benefit offerings provide employees the flexibility to choose the type of coverage that meets their individual needs. In addition, our associates may be eligible for paid leave including Paid Sick Leave or any other paid leave required by Federal, State, or local law, as well as Holiday pay where applicable.\\n\\nEqual Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled\\n\\nMilitary connected talent encouraged to apply\\n\\nTo read our Candidate Privacy Information Statement, which explains how we will use your information, please navigate to https://www.akkodis.com/en/us/candidate-privacy-policy\\n\\nThe Company will consider qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records in accordance with federal, state, and local laws and/or security clearance requirements, including, as applicable:\\n• The California Fair Chance Act\\n• Los Angeles City Fair Chance Ordinance\\n• Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers\\n• San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance\\n\\nMassachusetts Candidates Only: It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.","1 day ago","2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z",["215","216","221"],["217","218","222"],"https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DEgCzjQDRSADDZ8E1AAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"EgCzjQDRSADDZ8E1AAAAAA==","","Front End Developer -- PRADC5840839","Compunnel Inc.","https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSkm1XE9pXWO7v2AD8Rf3eKCCdR0KgG1couVmYG&s=0","https://www.compunnel.com",["213"],"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/front-end-developer-pradc5840839-at-compunnel-inc-4446813460",["226"],"We're looking for a Front End Developer to join our team and help deliver engaging, accessible, and user-friendly digital experiences.\\n\\nIf you enjoy working with HTML, CSS, and Content Management Systems (CMS) while collaborating with marketing and business teams to create exceptional web experiences, we'd love to hear from you.\\n\\nWhat You'll Do:\\n• Maintain and enhance website content and functionality\\n• Develop and update web pages using HTML and CSS\\n• Publish and manage content through a CMS\\n• Ensure websites meet accessibility standards (WCAG/Section 508)\\n• Apply SEO best practices to improve content visibility\\n• Test website functionality across browsers and devices\\n• Support website enhancements and digital initiatives\\n\\nWe're Looking For:\\n• Experience with HTML and CSS\\n• Familiarity with CMS platforms (WordPress, Drupal, Sitecore, AEM, SharePoint, etc.)\\n• Knowledge of SEO and web accessibility\\n• Strong attention to detail\\n• A proactive, self-driven mindset with excellent collaboration skills","3 days ago","2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z","https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DPZtDsEXLCZBELfISAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"PZtDsEXLCZBELfISAAAAAA==","","Senior React.js Software Engineer","Ecological network of Ukraine, PO",["219"],"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/senior-react-js-software-engineer-at-ecological-network-of-ukraine-po-4445083781",["227"],"• Home\\n• The Team\\n• News\\n• About Organisation expand_more\\n• Vision and Mission\\n• Ukraine-Visegrad\\n• Partnership\\n• Donation\\n• Українська\\n• English\\n• Українська\\n• English\\n• mail support@ecological.org.ua\\n• phone_in_talk +38 (044) 221-01-69\\n• Home\\n• The Team\\n• News\\n• About Organisation expand_more\\n• Vision and Mission\\n• Ukraine-Visegrad\\n• Partnership\\n• Donation\\n• Українська\\n• English\\n• language\\n• Українська\\n• English\\n• more_vert\\n• mail support@ecological.org.ua\\n• phone_in_talk +38 (044) 221-01-69\\n•\\n\\nSenior React.js Software Engineer\\n\\nlocation_on Chicago\\n\\nDirections: Software Development\\n\\nOverview\\n\\nLorem ipsum dolor sit amet, qui tollit laoreet ocurreret id, ne vis melius offendit appetere, ius timeam percipit argumentum id. His mutat nostrum ad, ei qui nostro aeterno recteque, aperiam quaerendum id has. Quod tantas volumus eu eum, mei appetere honestatis an.\\n\\nLorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Eum, rerum. Nisi harum nam id quasi officia sed placeat deleniti nulla. Consectetur aspernatur dicta animi iste cum rerum officia dolorum consequatur? Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Vel quod nam corporis alias et eum laboriosam sed, quisquam eligendi, harum repellat enim adipisci facilis blanditiis nulla quaerat assumenda accusantium.\\n\\nMain Responsibilities\\n\\n• Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, qui tollit\\n• laoreet ocurreret id, ne vis melius\\n• offendit appetere, ius timeam percipit\\n• argumentum id. His mutat\\n\\nWe Offer\\n\\n• Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, qui tollit\\n• laoreet ocurreret id, ne vis melius\\n• offendit appetere, ius timeam percipit\\n• argumentum id. His mutat\\n\\nApply\\n\\nFirst Name *\\n\\nLast Name *\\n\\nPhone *\\n\\nEmail *\\n\\nAttack CV *\\n\\nAdditional comments\\n\\nI agree to the transfer of personal data in accordance with the Privacy Policy\\n\\nJill Peterson\\n\\nHR Manager","https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DRL-xdc7eAxlRFM37AAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"RL-xdc7eAxlRFM37AAAAAA==","","Senior Developer - IT",["219"],"https://careers.united.com/us/en/job/WHQ00026570/Senior-Developer-IT",["228"],"Achieving our goals starts with supporting yours. Grow your career, access top-tier health and wellness benefits, build lasting connections with your team and our customers, and travel the world using our extensive route network.\\n\\nCome join us to create what’s next. Let’s define tomorrow, together.\\n\\nDescription\\n\\nUnited's Digital Technology team is comprised of many talented individuals all working together with cutting-edge technology to build the best airline in the history of aviation. Our team designs, develops and maintains massively scaling technology solutions brought to life with innovative architectures, data analytics, and digital solutions.\\n\\nJob overview and responsibilities\\n\\nThe Senior Software Developer will be responsible for the development of critical applications, while working with a team of developers. This role will design, develop, document, test and debug new and existing applications. Additionally, this role will build these applications with a focus on delivering cloud-based solutions. The individual will use groundbreaking technologies and enterprise grade integration software daily and will be relied upon to help take the team to the next level from a technological standpoint.\\n• Manages and participates in full development life cycle including requirements analysis and design using Agile methodologies\\n• Serve as technical expert on development projects\\n• Write technical specifications based on conceptual design and stated business requirements\\n• Support, maintain, and document software functionality\\n• Identify and evaluate new technologies for implementation\\n• Analyze code to find causes of errors and revise programs as needed\\n• Managers and participates in software design meetings and analyze user needs to determine technical requirements\\n• Collaborate & lead tech teams consisting of employees & vendor company contractors in planning and execution, serving as an technology leader\\n• Collaborate with end user to prototype, refine, test, and debug programs to meet needs\\nQualifications\\n\\nWhat’s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\\n• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Management Information Systems or related field\\n• 5+ years of experience in design, development, documenting, testing, and debugging of new and existing software systems and/or applications for market sale or large-scale proprietary software for internal use in an agile environment\\n• 5+ years’ experience implementing AWS technologies (Lambda, Step Functions, CloudWatch, CloudFront, Cognito, route53, Dynamo DB, ECS, EC2, S3, RDS, API Gateway)\\n• Experience with Cloud Automation Development Tool such as Git, Python/Bash/PowerShell Scripting\\n• Hands-on development and proficient excellence in backend API development using Node.js Java and Python (nice to have)\\n• Strong knowledge of Java, SQL, NoSQL and Design Patterns.\\n• Excellent knowledge of Object-Oriented systems design and Application Development\\n• Must be legally authorized to work in the United States for any employer without sponsorship\\n• Successful completion of interview required to meet job qualification\\n• Reliable, punctual attendance is an essential function of the position\\n\\nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\\n• Airlines industry experience is a plus\\n• AWS highly preferred\\n\\nThe base pay range for this role is $112,480.00 to $146,540.00.\\nThe base salary range/hourly rate listed is dependent on job-related, factors such as experience, education, and skills. This position is also eligible for bonus and/or long-term incentive compensation awards.\\n\\nYou may be eligible for the following competitive benefits: medical, dental, vision, life, accident & disability, parental leave, employee assistance program, commuter, paid holidays, paid time off, 401(k) and flight privileges.\\n\\nUnited Airlines is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We recruit, employ, train, compensate, and promote without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. We provide reasonable accommodations for applicants and employees with disabilities. To request an accommodation, contact JobAccommodations@united.com","2 days ago","2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z",["215","216","221"],["217","218","222"],"https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DGLA8czDfU_KzjnxbAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer",{},"GLA8czDfU_KzjnxbAAAAAA==","","初级软件工程师","Solar Digital Agro LLC","https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSjHYOnyjGHzrvaajpKOjoh4jtrTudHazw1qmz5&s=0",["219"],"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/%E5%88%9D%E7%BA%A7%E8%BD%AF%E4%BB%B6%E5%B7%A5%E7%A8%8B%E5%B8%88-at-solar-digital-agro-llc-4447512722",["229"],"Location: Chicago, Illinois\\n\\nExperience: 0–2 years\\n\\nEmployment Type: Full-time\\n\\nVisa Sponsorship: Available for qualified candidates\\n\\nWe are looking for an early-career Software Engineer who is interested in financial markets, real-time systems, trading infrastructure, and data engineering.\\n\\nThis is a hands-on, zero-to-one opportunity. You will help us build a practical and reliable trading system from the ground up, including order management, market data processing, risk controls, execution monitoring, and trading data infrastructure.\\n\\nDepending on your background and strengths, you may begin with either the trading execution system or the trading database and data infrastructure.\\n\\nWhat You’ll Work On\\n• Develop and maintain trading system components using C++ and Python\\n• Build order entry, order monitoring, execution confirmation, position tracking, and risk-control modules\\n• Integrate broker, exchange, market data, or trading APIs\\n• Design databases and data pipelines for market data, orders, executions, positions, P&L, and risk records\\n• Improve system performance, reliability, observability, and fault recovery\\n• Develop logging, reconciliation, monitoring, alerting, and reporting tools\\n• Work closely with traders and quantitative researchers to turn trading requirements into reliable software\\n• Test, document, troubleshoot, and continuously improve production workflows\\n\\nMinimum Qualifications\\n• 0–2 years of professional experience; new graduates are welcome to apply\\n• Proficiency in both C++ and Python\\n• Solid understanding of data structures, algorithms, object-oriented programming, and software engineering fundamentals\\n• Familiarity with SQL, databases, Linux, Git, and basic networking concepts\\n• Ability to write clear, maintainable, and testable code\\n• Strong attention to detail and willingness to troubleshoot real operational problems\\n• Ability to communicate professionally in either English or Mandarin; bilingual ability is welcome but not required\\n\\nPreferred Qualifications\\n• Experience contributing to a large software project through employment, internships, academic research, open-source work, or personal projects\\n• Experience with multithreading, asynchronous programming, real-time systems, or performance optimization\\n• Familiarity with trading systems, OMS/EMS platforms, broker APIs, exchange connectivity, or financial market data\\n• Experience with PostgreSQL, TimescaleDB, Redis, Kafka, or other high-volume data technologies\\n• Knowledge of futures, equities, options, order books, risk controls, or the trade lifecycle\\n• Experience building monitoring, reconciliation, logging, or fault-tolerant systems\\n• Strong interest in financial markets and trading technology\\n\\nWhat We Offer\\n• The opportunity to build a trading platform from the ground up\\n• Direct exposure to traders, quantitative researchers, and real-world trading workflows\\n• Ownership of meaningful production projects at an early career stage\\n• Professional development in trading systems, data infrastructure, and quantitative technology\\n• Competitive compensation and performance-based growth opportunities\\n• Visa sponsorship support for qualified candidates\\n• A collaborative workplace that welcomes candidates from all backgrounds","18 hours ago","2026-07-31T14:00:00.000Z","https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3D52ihPcrbknU2BIEwAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer","4K–6K a month","MONTH",{},"52ihPcrbknU2BIEwAAAAAA==","","Principal Software Developer - Full Stack (Unity, C#)","Zynga","https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcThyjPIJATVijA7R8dB_JKzjRy12PizeA8aUAUu&s=0","https://www.zynga.com","Indeed",["219"],"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=c5d4e7c24aafa8d4",["230"],"Level Up Your Career with Zynga!\\n\\nAt Zynga, we bring people together through the power of play. As a global leader in interactive entertainment and a proud label of Take-Two Interactive, our games have been downloaded over 6 billion times—connecting players in 175+ countries through fun, strategy, and a little friendly competition.\\n\\nFrom thrilling casino spins to epic strategy battles, mind-bending puzzles, and social word challenges, our diverse game portfolio has something for everyone. Fan-favorites and latest hits include FarmVille™, Words With Friends™, Zynga Poker™, Game of Thrones Slots Casino™, Wizard of Oz Slots™, Hit it Rich! Slots™, Wonka Slots™, Top Eleven™, Toon Blast™, Empires & Puzzles™, Merge Dragons!™, CSR Racing™, Harry Potter: Puzzles & Spells™, Match Factory™, and Color Block Jam™—plus many more!\\n\\nFounded in 2007 and headquartered in California, our teams span North America, Europe, and Asia, working together to craft unforgettable gaming experiences. Whether you're spinning, strategizing, matching, or competing, Zynga is where fun meets innovation—and where you can take your career to the next level.\\n\\nJoin us and be part of the play!\\n\\nPosition Overview:\\n\\nZynga is looking for a Principal Software Engineer level in the Austin, Eugene, Toronto, San Mateo, Carlsbad, or Chicago areas.\\n\\nThis position will be to develop and maintain the core client technology, engine-level systems, and infrastructure for a game with a cozy vibe targeting a casual audience. You should have a passion for engineering excellence and be comfortable diagnosing and solving deep, systemic technical problems, such as improving load times, frame rate, memory footprint, and other cross-cutting performance concerns. You'll need to operate with rigorous engineering discipline while working largely independently to plan and execute complex, multi-week technical initiatives.\\n\\nWe have a well-rounded, highly motivated, distributed team with a mission-driven culture working on a new game. We need a self-driven engineer who confronts challenges with optimism, communicates clearly and easily, and takes a great deal of pride in their work. You'll have an opportunity to own core engine and infrastructure work, including upgrading and maintaining third-party libraries and dependencies, evolving build and tooling pipelines, and making foundational changes to the client architecture that unlock future feature roadmaps for the rest of the engineering team.\\n\\nWhat You'll Do:\\n\\n•\\nDefine, architect, and develop core systems and client infrastructure in Unity and C#\\n\\n•\\nDiagnose and resolve complex, game-wide technical issues such as slow load times, low frame rates, memory pressure, and build/runtime stability\\n\\n•\\nOwn the evaluation, upgrade, and maintenance of third-party libraries, SDKs, and engine dependencies\\n\\n•\\nDesign and implement foundational architecture changes that enable future feature roadmaps for feature-focused engineers to build upon\\n\\n•\\nProduce technical design documentation and implementation plans for infrastructure and systemic initiatives\\n\\n•\\nScope and cost work accurately from loosely defined requirements, presenting estimates with clear assumptions and identified risks\\n\\n•\\nAdapt plans and technical approaches when requirements or platform constraints change\\n\\n•\\nReview code, technical design documentation, and implementation plans for other team members\\n\\n•\\nProactively profile, optimize, and refactor code to meet team performance and stability KPI goals\\n\\n•\\nExplore, develop, and integrate new technologies and tools that benefit the broader engineering team\\n\\n•\\nWork closely with other engineers to lead multi-week or month-long infrastructure and tooling efforts\\n\\n•\\nGive team and divisional tech talks on architectures that you've built\\n\\n•\\nWork to improve and evolve team process and engineering standards\\n\\n•\\nHelp to mentor other engineers\\n\\nWhat You Bring:\\n\\n•\\nB.Sc. in Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent education / work experience\\n\\n•\\n6+ Years game industry / mobile app experience as a software developer\\n\\n•\\nShipped titles and/or live games experience, especially mobile (iOS / Android)\\n\\n•\\nExpert knowledge in C#\\n\\n•\\n3+ Years Unity experience, including engine-level and low-level systems work\\n\\n• A solid understanding of client/server architecture in modern mobile games\\n\\n• Understanding, interest and knowledge of server-side architecture in mobile games\\n\\n•\\nSolid foundation in data structures, algorithms and software methodologies\\n\\n•\\nDemonstrated experience diagnosing and resolving performance issues such as load times, frame rate, and memory usage\\n\\n•\\nExperience upgrading, integrating, or maintaining third-party libraries, SDKs, or engine versions\\n\\n•\\nExperience with the AWS ecosystem, Kubernetes, and back end monitoring technologies such as Datadog\\n\\n•\\nExcellent communication skills and comfort working in a collaborative environment\\n\\n•\\nExcellent ability to foresee and proactively resolve blockers, technical risk, and points of failure\\n\\n•\\nExcellent ability to function in an asynchronous distributed work environment while still tuning in to key team meetings\\n\\n•\\nExperience with git\\n\\n•\\nExperience with performance profiling and optimization tools\\n\\nBonus Points:\\n\\n•\\nExperience with Unity engine source modification or custom engine forks\\n\\n•\\nExperience with build pipeline, CI/CD, or dev tooling for game teams\\n\\n•\\nExperience playing and working on games that target a casual audience\\n\\n•\\nExperience using Claude Code or a similar AI coding tool\\n\\nWhat We Offer You:\\n\\nZynga offers a world-class benefits package that helps support and balance the needs of our teams. To find out more about our benefits, visit the Zynga Benefits site\\n\\nThe pay range for this position in Toronto at the start of employment is expected to be between $114,300 and $164,300 per Year. However, base pay offered is based on market location, and may vary further depending on individualized factors for job candidates, such as job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and other objective business considerations.\\n\\nThe pay range for this position in California at the start of employment is expected to be between $133,900 and $180,000 per Year. However, base pay offered is based on market location, and may vary further depending on individualized factors for job candidates, such as job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and other objective business considerations.\\n\\nThe pay range for this position in Illinois at the start of employment is expected to be between $120,600 and $170,000 per Year. However, base pay offered is based on market location, and may vary further depending on individualized factors for job candidates, such as job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and other objective business considerations.\\n\\nSubject to those same considerations, the total compensation package for this position may also include other elements, including a bonus and/or equity awards and eligibility to participate in our 401(K) plan and Employee Stock Purchase Program.\\n\\nRegular, full-time employees are also eligible for a range of benefits at the Company, including: medical, dental, vision, and basic life insurance coverage; 14 paid holidays per calendar year; paid vacation time per calendar year (ranging from 15 to 25 days) or eligibility to participate in the Company's discretionary time off program; up to 10 paid sick days per calendar year; paid parental and compassionate leave; wellbeing programs for mental health and other wellness support; family planning support through Maven; commuter benefits; and reimbursements for fitness-related expenses. The use of Artificial Intelligence is not being used to screen candidates. The position is for an existing vacancy.\\n\\nWe are proud to be an equal opportunity employer, which means we are committed to creating and celebrating diverse thoughts, cultures, and backgrounds throughout our organization. Employment with us is based on substantive ability, objective qualifications, and work ethic – not an individual's race, creed, color, religion, sex or gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin or ancestry, alienage or citizenship status, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, status as a victim of domestic violence or sex offenses, reproductive health decision, or any other characteristics protected by applicable law.\\n\\nAs an equal opportunity employer, we are committed to providing the necessary support and accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities, health conditions, or impairments (subject to any local qualifying requirements) to ensure their full participation in the job application or interview process. Please contact us at accommodationrequest@zynga.com to request any accommodations or for support related to your application for an open position.\\n\\nPlease be aware that Zynga does not conduct job interviews or make job offers over third-party messaging apps such as Telegram, WhatsApp, or others. Zynga also does not engage in any financial exchanges during the recruitment or onboarding process, and will never ask a candidate for their personal or financial information over an app or other unofficial chat channel. Any attempt to do so may be the result of a scamp or phishing attack, and you should not engage. Zynga's in-house recruitment team will only contact individuals through their official Company email addresses (i.e., via a zynga.com, take2games.com, naturalmotion.com, smallgiantgames.com, themavens.com, gram.gs email domain).","18 days ago","2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z",["216","221","215"],["218","222","217"],"https://www.google.com/search?q=jobs&gl=us&hl=en&udm=8#vhid=vt%3D20/docid%3DcbG_xTcnuiygUvjlAAAAAA%3D%3D&vssid=jobs-detail-viewer","114K–164K a year","YEAR",{},"cbG_xTcnuiygUvjlAAAAAA==","CONTRACTOR",{"apply_link":"68","is_direct":false,"publisher":"65"},"health_insurance","dental_coverage","Health insurance","Dental insurance","FULLTIME",{"apply_link":"90","is_direct":false,"publisher":"87"},"paid_time_off","Paid time off",{"apply_link":"106","is_direct":false,"publisher":"65"},{"apply_link":"118","is_direct":false,"publisher":"65"},{"apply_link":"132","is_direct":false,"publisher":"130"},{"apply_link":"148","is_direct":false,"publisher":"65"},{"apply_link":"160","is_direct":false,"publisher":"65"},{"apply_link":"169","is_direct":false,"publisher":"87"},{"apply_link":"184","is_direct":false,"publisher":"65"},{"apply_link":"201","is_direct":false,"publisher":"199"}]	\N
